research/audit/wave12-dispatch/certifier-a6-ex-componentwise-convergence-and-a-vector-valued-integral-computed-r2.prompt.md:443:  "rationale": "Lebl, Section 7.3.2, Proposition 7.3.9 states that convergence of a sequence in Euclidean space is equivalent to coordinatewise convergence; APEX Calculus, Theorem 12.2.32, defines the definite integral of a vector-valued function componentwise. The item combines those standard interfaces in a zero-indexed R^3 example, computes the polynomial Riemann integral locally through the library's scalar FTC interfaces, and proves its strict Euclidean-norm estimate locally. The supplied numbered argument was audited as a local proof rather than a transcription or identifiable adaptation of a source proof.",
